 "root_cause": "Skill notice queried its first active catalog before _execute admission. Closed/full services could still query, the initial query bypassed the two execution slots and eight owned-operation limit, and cancellation of its delivery waiter left no service task to drain. Later package reads were already owned.",
 "changes": [
  "Move the initial catalog query and empty-result return into the existing owned perform operation",
  "Apply close/full admission before first I/O and charge the initial query to the existing two execution slots/eight pending operations",
  "Keep admitted catalog/revision/package/authorization reads owned across caller or close-waiter cancellation, so lifecycle retains database/parser/object resources until real work finishes",
  "Do not re-admit later read stages during draining; empty catalogs still avoid parsing",
  "Preserve captured revision/order, exact instruction payload, final revocation check, failure propagation, limits and close timeouts"
 ],
